    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d795">

                <pb facs="0744" n="732" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg732"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R/1051: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-13T23:00:00-04:00">May 13, 1940—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. Your 66, May 13, 6 p.m. The text of the Uruguayan draft is being telegraphed
                        tonight<anchor n="61" xml:id="d795-f1"/> to our missions in the 11 countries
                    specified in your telegram under reference with the request that it be placed
                    promptly before the Governments concerned and that the latter cable their reply
                    to the President of Panama without delay. It is being indicated at the same time
                    that the Government of the United States is in full agreement with the text.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
